<title>RUSSIA: Brake fluid kills two Kazakh soldiers.</title>
<headline>Brake fluid kills two Kazakh soldiers.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two Kazakh conscripts died and 12 others were seriously ill after drinking brake fluid, Itar-Tass news agency said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The soldiers each drank a glass of the fluid, made from ethylene glycol rather than spirits, at a military base in the town of Balkhash on Saturday night, the Kazakh Defence Ministry told Tass.</p>
<p>The sick conscripts were in serious condition at a detoxification unit in Almaty, the Kazakh capital, Tass said.</p>
